WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.200
Language is the foundation of culture and&nbsp;
technology. The uniquely human power to implant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:11.040
complex thoughts into each other's minds, just&nbsp;
by making sounds, gestures, or marks on paper.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:16.160
It's a feat of such staggering sophistication that&nbsp;
the world's most advanced supercomputers can't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:22.080
compete with the proficiency of a three-year-old&nbsp;
child. We use this ability all day, every day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:27.760
but rarely stop to think about how incredible&nbsp;
it is. I'm Dr. Rrica Brozovsky, sociolinguist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:32.880
and certified word nerd, and I've always been&nbsp;
fascinated with language. Behind every word&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:37.280
and figure of speech is a story about where&nbsp;
we came from and how we relate to each other.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:44.000
Join me as we stop to really listen to what we&nbsp;
say and why we say it--an investigation that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:57.040
will span the fields of history, biology,&nbsp;
pop culture, and more. On Otherwords!

